            <div xml:id="d672">

                <pb facs="1230" n="1106" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1106"/>

                <head>No. 668.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 10, 1881</date>.
                        (Received January 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 326.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Gazette de Lausanne of Friday evening
                    contains a notice to the effect that the commune of Gersau, in the canton of
                    Sehwytz, is, owing to the scarcity of work, compelled to assist its citizens to
                    emigrate, and that it has voted a subsidy of 250 francs to those over eighteen
                    years who emigrate, and 100 francs to their children over ten, and 30 francs to
                    those under ten years of age.</p>
                <p>The Bund of this morning contains a similar statement. I inclose copies of both
                    of these notices, with translations thereof herewith.</p>
                <p>I have instructed Consul Byers to inquire and report concerning the action of the
                    authorities of Gersau.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>NICHOLAS FISH.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d672-a1.xml" xpointer="d672-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
